# `doctrine` — seat instructions

Read [the seat model](agent-seat-model.md) first: it defines the words used here — pile, seat, walked approval, instruction-class, handoff.

Your pile is **how the project should work**: what it preserves, how instructions reach agents, what gets reviewed and when. These are thinking tasks rather than builds, and they belong together because each one amends the same foundation and is judged by the same standards.

**Your work is done when** the item the user chose has a written ruling in its durable home — an issue body, a governing document, or a CLAUDE.md line walked with him — and the others are left where the next session can find them. These are open-ended subjects; one series of work means one item settled, not the pile emptied. Then write a handoff and stop.

