# nedschorus Boot-Up Plan

The preparation the boss + new-vp (the old system's VP agent) do to bring choirmaster into existence. The boss works one step at a time; this is the order of steps with what each produces. The first task choirmaster will run is deliberately the LAST step. This is the founding pair's workflow document — the specifications it points at are written for zero-context readers; this file is written for us.

## Standing decisions (all boss-ruled, 2026-07-20/21; provenance in git history and the machine-local founding transcripts — deliberately uncommitted, open question 2)

- Fresh repo `~/Projects/nedschorus` (live: https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus — owned by the `nedschorus` organization since 2026-07-21; the old `nedlern/nedschorus` URL redirects). The old project is LEGACY: read-only reference; every import crosses the entry checkpoint — recorded in the importing commit's `Gatekeeper-import` trailer, same commit (browsable via `git-gatekeeper.py imports`; `entry-manifest.md` is the founding-era record, no longer appended — boss-walked ruling 2026-07-24), hand-recorded during the founding window (the manual rung), enforced by the git-gatekeeper from choirmaster's day one (the git-gatekeeper is its first build task; boss-ruled scoping 2026-07-21, package-review S5).
- Primary agent: **choirmaster** (Claude runtime), running with bypass permissions (`.claude/settings.json` → `permissions.defaultMode: bypassPermissions`).
- **The git-gatekeeper** is the permanent check-in architecture — one program holding the project's one push-capable credential is the only gate to main; every agent invokes it directly and none pushes; all checks live at the gate from day one (boss-walked revision 2026-07-24). Specification: [git-gatekeeper-design.md](git-gatekeeper-design.md) ([nedschorus#3](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/3)); renamed from fast-pr-to-prod-design 2026-07-24 — the design's scope ends at main; deployment is a separate DevOps/CI concern.
- **Git-gatekeeper rulings 2026-07-21 (all in the specification):** the account layout, org form, applied LIVE — the repo lives in the `nedschorus` organization; both boss accounts are org owners (`NedLern` — also the machine/agent credential and the only permitted pusher — and `NedLerner`, settings and emergency power, no push); branch protection on `main` with enforce-admins, force-push and deletion blocked; the boss never commits directly. Check-table additions adopted from the prior-art cross-check: exact-tree validation, trailer-schema provenance record, declared-vs-actual paths, replay protection, and the executable legacy-import command (one-transaction copy + digests + import-trailer write; one component per check-in).
- **The publishing program** ([nedschorus#4](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/4)): strategy admitted and walked in full; `nedschorus.com` is **registered** (the boss, 2026-07-21); every further external action — account, site, first post — waits on a per-action go; the first build step is deliberately unpicked while the boss deliberates.
- **The prior-art cross-check is complete** — two adversarial passes over the nine founding patterns; every borrowing's disposition is recorded on closed [nedschorus#5](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/5), and the full reports are git-history-recoverable from there (the doc was temporary reference, disposed at close). Net: git-gatekeeper/ladder/python-first are established practice (validating, not novel); the handoff governance bundle and legacy-with-manifest survived as unmatched compositions; handoff-quality instrumentation deferred low-priority with raise-triggers ([nedschorus#6](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/6)).
- **The handoff system** — session recycling (revised 2026-08-02, superseding the drafts-and-committed-series form): verbatim dialog carry from a quoted boundary, supervisor-driven kill-and-relaunch, machine-local and disposable, tasks migrated by pre-seed; git — the repo's ordinary committed content — is the long-term record; one committed handoff exists, the founding one. Specification: [fast-handoff-design.md](fast-handoff-design.md) ([nedschorus#2](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/2)). Skill named `handoff`.
- **The Codex companion arrives early** — right after choirmaster's boot test passes, in advisory mode: it drafts freely in its own clone, never pushes, no git identity ever; its work is checked in via promotion (attribution by provenance stamp). Two channels compose for the pair: **MCP as the call channel, one-off OR threaded** — each CLI exposes itself as an MCP server (Codex-direction measured 2026-07-21; Claude-direction via `claude mcp serve`, unprobed); a fresh call spawns a new instance (right for consults, reviews, ask-both-heads-the-same-thing), and a THREAD sustains a real multi-turn discussion with context intact (Codex: `codex-reply` with a thread id; Claude: `claude -p --resume <session-id>` — whether resume keeps or forks the session id is unprobed). Threading reaches the conversation, not the live terminal: it neither displays in nor wakes a peer's interactive window. **Mini-comms (a second two-log-file bridge)** therefore keeps only what it is uniquely good at: asynchronous, boss-readable coordination that survives either side's death. The parallel-proposal workbench UI is a recorded future candidate. **Companion continuity (boss-ruled 2026-07-21, package-review S3):** the Codex runtime's persistent session IS the mechanism — auto-compaction keeps one session viable indefinitely (fleet-observed on the old system's CDX agents), and `codex exec resume <session-id>` re-enters it with context intact (measured twice, 2026-07-21). No Codex-side handoff adapter is built. Accepted residual (boss-ruled 2026-07-21): companion context lives in machine-local `~/.codex/sessions` rollouts with no committed handoff fallback, so a lost or corrupted session loses its context — not a concern here because companion work is advisory and every durable output is checked in via promotion; reopening trigger: a companion session loss that costs real work.
- 100% manual edit-production pipeline; automation earned rung by rung (manual → script-you-run → automation). Python liberally, and light: python over prompts, python over bash; smallness kept by re-derivation, the single door, and earned complexity — not by the language.
- CLAUDE.md lines settled so far: the handoff pickup line; the transcript-archive pointer; commit-as-you-go with session id in every commit message; the zero-context-reader writing rule for durable artifacts (delivered inside every writing skill too); the check-in timing rule ([nedschorus#25](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/25) — post-boot needs live as GHIs, not standing decisions; boss-ruled 2026-07-24).
- **Terminology (boss-ruled 2026-07-24, twice-extended):** use standard SDLC terms; never invent vocabulary. The check-in gate component class is the **gatekeeper**; this one, being git-specific, is the **git-gatekeeper** (other gatekeepers may exist later) — the former name "throat" is retired. The old system is **legacy**, never "quarry". The operation of getting a change onto main is a **check-in** (`git-gatekeeper.py check-in`) — the former "land"/"landing" is retired. The agent instruction file is called by its name, **CLAUDE.md** — the former "kernel" is retired (a kernel is an OS component). And the framing: NC is **not a rebuild** of the old system — it starts from its own requirements and cherry-picks pieces of nedlern that earn entry through the checkpoint.
- **Public-links policy (boss-ruled 2026-07-24, outer walk item 14):** this repository is public, and links in it are judged on usefulness and reliability only — there is no provenance-based quarantine class. Unofficial or leaked archives may be linked and used like any other source when they offer documentation or insight not available elsewhere; claims derived from them carry the normal reliability record (provenance varies, so: model, surface, version/date, extraction method, confidence); and unofficial extractions are never runtime contracts or dependencies — a reliability judgment about unversioned snapshots of a moving product, not a provenance one (accepted principle 4 of the pair-#9 notes).
- **The rewrite policy (boss-ruled 2026-07-24, outer walk item 13):** governs every legacy cherry-pick. At the moment work reads legacy material — an import crossing the checkpoint, or a build slice using legacy code as reference — the builder classifies exactly the legacy features that work touches, each into one of four classes: **preserve-feature** (the feature's contract survives, probably not its implementation — the implementation is re-derived unless the import record separately justifies keeping it; every preserve claim is named and test-pinned, so compatibility is demonstrated, not assumed), **update-feature** (the feature survives changed; the divergence is recorded so nobody later "fixes" NC back toward legacy behavior), **remove-feature** (the feature does not come along; a one-line reason is recorded — saying "defective" when that is the reason, so a removed defect cannot sneak back in via a later pick), **consider-feature** (not decidable now; blocks nothing; re-decided the moment work depends on it). No global inventory of legacy behavior is ever built — classification is per cherry-pick. The record lives in the slice plan's classification table or the entry-manifest line; a consider-feature that outlives its slice moves to [`legacy-feature-queue/`](#project-organization) — never a GHI, which is reserved for things we think we want. Default: **unexamined is never preserved** — silence about a legacy feature means NC does not have it; "legacy did it" is never a requirement without a recorded preserve-feature. Enforcement rung: discipline now; the `plan-rewrite-slice` skill ([nedschorus#16](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/16)) embeds the procedure when built.
- The boss's review queue is **issues labeled `draft`** (boss-ruled 2026-07-24, renaming `boss-review`: a marker names the artifact's STATE, not the action owed — a queued issue IS a draft; the label is the issue-world's queue membership under the artifact-lifecycle rule, § Project organization) — same format as all issues, full-context walkable bodies, non-blocking by rule, no title/filename markers (the label is the single authority). The scrub step of each handoff states every queue's depth AND oldest item's age — the `draft` issue queue and the directory queues alike — so starvation is visible, not just volume (package-review item 9; drain procedure tracked on [nedschorus#24](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/24)). When issue creation fails, the routed body is kept durably (committed) until an issue id exists — a routed suggestion is never lost to a failed API call.
- Boot-pack validation is boot-testing the delta with genuinely fresh subagents, not review alone. A fresh subagent's context floor (CLAUDE.md + prompt) is the measured boot state of every future reader.

## Project organization

The full preservation-and-placement design — what NC preserves (four
classes), where each class goes, how the rules become code and skills, and
the drift-prevention sweep — is the pair
[nedschorus#32](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/32)
([docs/issues/32-preservation-and-placement.md](../issues/32-preservation-and-placement.md)),
boss-walked 2026-07-27/28; it graduates to a wiki page with subpages when
matured. This section holds the directory homes and the artifact-lifecycle
rule the pair builds on.

Five committed homes plus the shared place — no `docs/working/` ever exists:

1. **`docs/wiki/`** — permanent truth (Obsidian vault; `.obsidian/` gitignored, matching the legacy system's practice — config is per-vault, so the old wiki cannot be affected). Its `queue/` subdirectory holds wiki-bound doctrine awaiting the boss's drain (artifact-lifecycle rule, below).
2. **`docs/issues/<n>-<slug>.md`** — working material, one document per substantial issue; header carries the issue link only (the issue's open/closed state is the sole status authority). At issue close, the same commit disposes the document three ways (boss-ruled 2026-07-22, superseding the 2026-07-21 delete-or-promote form; pair #5's deletion stands as history): the DEFAULT is complete-and-archive — stamp frontmatter (`completed: <date>` + disposition) and move to `docs/issues/archived/`, so the active directory lists only open work; wiki PROMOTION is rare — only knowledge hard to reproduce by reading the files (a large system design, cross-cutting behavior no single file reveals), with `design-as-of:` frontmatter and the production-is-SSOT line; DELETE is nearly retired — only content that should not exist in the tree at all (the redaction class). Close is an ordered two-phase operation across two systems (package-review item 9): FIRST the disposing commit is checked in, THEN the issue closes referencing that commit. A failure between the phases leaves an open issue pointing at a disposed document — the visible half-state; recovery is finishing phase two (close the issue, referencing the commit), never re-opening the disposal. The reverse order is forbidden because its half-state — a closed issue with a live document — is invisible exactly where the status authority says nothing is pending. The choice between them (boss-ruled 2026-07-21): promote only distilled standing knowledge; an evidence archive or reference file DELETES, with the extracted decisions memorialized in their governing documents and a `git show <sha>:<path>` recovery pointer on the closing issue. The `queue/` subdirectory (`docs/issues/queue/`) holds pair-bound MDs awaiting the boss's drain (artifact-lifecycle rule, below).
3. **`handoff/`** — the numbered handoff series with transcripts.
4. **`docs/cross-project/`** — artifacts shared with the old system, including the founding documents (migrated here from the legacy system, frozen there at 78ed90f0).
5. **`nc-queue/`** — the tracked intake directory for boss-requested notes awaiting their initial walk (boss-ruled 2026-07-22). Every requested note is committed as `nc-queue/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<slug>.md`, and a note request is complete only when the file exists there. Queue commits are verbatim relays, never reviewed before being committed — the S1 residual class covers raw content on the public repository, and the drafting agent owns keeping do-not-publish material out (reopening trigger: a leak that costs something). At the note's initial walk the durable parts disperse to their homes — a GHI, an MD-GHI pair, a script, a REVISE on an existing artifact; the walk itself is never memorialized — and the dispersal commit MOVES the note to `nc-queue/archived/`, stamping frontmatter at that moment: `processed: <date>`, `dispositions: [<destinations>]`, `dropped-by: <author>` (boss-ruled 2026-07-22). An unwalked note expires at a 90-day TTL (boss-set), moved to `archived/` by the handoff scrub marked as expired; the scrub reports the queue root's count and oldest-note age at each handoff alongside the `draft`-issue numbers. Two dates, two homes: the DROP date is the filename date (set at creation — filesystem timestamps are never consulted; git does not preserve them), and the PROCESSED date is frontmatter. Unprocessed drops carry no frontmatter (verbatim capture, zero friction); frontmatter appears exactly at processing. The queue root empty means walks are caught up; `archived/` is the browsable processed history; git history additionally holds everything. Companion convention for LEDGER documents (pair docs, plans): a processed item is marked in place — `processed <date> → <outcome>` — with its body retained; documents dispose only at their ruled issue-close lifecycle. Frontmatter generally: a field exists only where a named consumer (a script or a reading pattern) uses it — no universal author/created stamps; git carries provenance.

6. **`legacy-feature-queue/`** — the decision queue for consider-features that outlive their slice (the rewrite policy, § Standing decisions). One file per feature, `legacy-feature-queue/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<slug>.md` — the date is when it was queued, giving the scrub its oldest-age without consulting filesystem timestamps (same convention as `nc-queue/`). Body: the feature in one paragraph, the legacy pin (SHA + path), the slice that hit it, why it is undecidable now, and what would decide it. Queued ONLY when still undecided at slice close — a consider-feature that resolves during its slice stays in the slice's classification table and never touches the queue, so every queue entry is a real open question. Drains by the standard four outcomes, and deciding IS the drain: promote to preserve-feature or update-feature (the GHI or slice-plan entry is minted then, when the feature becomes wanted), or remove-feature (file deleted, reason in the commit message). No TTL — a consider-feature blocks nothing; the scrub's depth + oldest-age report keeps starvation visible. The directory materializes in git at first use.

**The MD-GHI pair:** a request for a durable MD IS a request for a doc + issue pair (the boss's trigger word: "memorialize"). All NC-related GHIs — paired or issue-only — are filed on the nedschorus repository, never in the old system's tracker (boss-ruled 2026-07-22: NC context must not drown among the legacy system's thousands of issues). `md-write` searches existing pairs first, then disposes NEW / REVISE (default on subject match) / REPLACE (supersede, old issue closed same commit) / REMOVE; ambiguity goes to the `draft` issue queue, never blocks. Session provenance: MDs via commit messages; issues via a footer line. Revision convention (boss-ruled 2026-07-22): a clarification or revision to an issue or a pair document EDITS the artifact — the GHI body, the document — never a stacked clarifying comment; additive records multiply and conflict with what they meant to fix. Comments append only for genuinely new events (an instance outcome, a ruling challenge — "completion" collapsed into close-with-reason plus the body edit recording the outcome, user-ruled 2026-08-12). Append-only audit surfaces (review clearances and their trailers) are the deliberate exception. Artifact-lifecycle rule (boss-ruled 2026-07-24; supersedes and absorbs the 2026-07-23 three-state artifact rule): **every artifact is either final at its home, or sitting in a named queue that states its destination — and every queue has a drain process.** No stateless piles, ever. Destination known up front → destination-rooted queue: wiki-bound doctrine in `docs/wiki/queue/`, pair-bound MDs in `docs/issues/queue/` — the same `queue` token everywhere, so one grep finds every queue. Destination decided only at the drain → decision queue: `nc-queue/` (boss notes) and `legacy-feature-queue/` (undecided legacy features). Draft GHIs carry the **`draft` label** — the issue-world's queue membership, symmetric with the directories. The drain is one process for all queues ([nedschorus#24](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/24)): the boss walks a queue when he chooses; each item gets exactly one of four outcomes — **promote** (`git mv` to the destination; the move commit is the record), **edit** (revise, stays queued), **demote** (down to evidence/transient, attached to its pair or session), **drop** (deleted with the reason in the commit message — explicit, never silent rot). The handoff scrub step reports every queue's depth and oldest item; until the NC handoff skill is built, that reporting runs as discipline. Transient design/research MDs never enter these queues — they live and die attached to their pair or session. The absorbed three-state routing still governs write time: a queue drop needs NO GHI — the queue is its attention surface until the drain decides its fate, and minting a GHI at drop time front-runs the walk; the moment something is wanted as a feature, component, or commitment — any pending state — it gets a GHI (lean decision → issue-only; substantial working material → the MD-GHI pair: the MD carries the greppable substance, the GHI carries the walkable state); a bare MD with no GHI is legitimate only for final reference content awaiting nothing (operator notes beside code, wiki pages), and anything about it that later becomes pending gets a GHI then. Discriminator: the GHI carries state, the MD carries substance, the queue holds the not-yet-decided. Boss clarification 2026-07-25 (walk 17 cluster 2): **a committed doc is not an attention surface** — a backlog section or "captured research" note in a pair doc is a pile unless it is queued or carried by a GHI; anything task-shaped (an investigation, an evaluation, a build) gets a GHI even when small — lean bundled issues are fine; and agent-internal task lists are invisible to the boss until a review method exists ([nedschorus#28](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/28) item 5), so nothing may live only there. Enforced at write time by `ghi-write`/`md-write` ([nedschorus#13](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/13)).

**Accepted residuals (boss-ruled 2026-07-21):** when the boss overrides a review objection — accepts a risk, declines a mitigation — the artifact records it at the decision point as a named block: `Accepted residual (boss-ruled <date>):` the objection in one line, why it is not a concern for this project, and the reopening trigger (the evidence class that would legitimately re-raise it). Reviewer instructions carry the standing counterpart rule: a recorded accepted residual is re-flagged only with new evidence matching its trigger, filed as a separate RULING CHALLENGE, never as an ordinary finding. One grep on `Accepted residual` returns every such decision. The `md-write` and `d-review` skills embed both halves at build.

**Subsystem structure:** co-locate when free; subsystem subdirectories inside pinned roots at the second file; the subsystem token verbatim in every name (one grep returns the whole subsystem); a hygiene script (a git-gatekeeper check) verifies tokens and subdirectory moves — test-naming rules are enforced at writing time by the writing skills, not at the git-gatekeeper (claim corrected, package-review item 9) — placement itself stays the writer's judgment; a never-seen token routes to a `draft` issue.

## The steps

**1. Assemble the starting skills — FIVE** — every skill build follows [skill-authoring-checklist.md](../wiki/queue/skill-authoring-checklist.md) (content boss-approved 2026-07-24, outer walk item 11; queued at `docs/wiki/queue/` awaiting the wiki drain; every candidate-skill GHI carries the same pointer)**:** d-review and walk-me-through (legacy trims through the checkpoint); the handoff skill; `ghi-write` (issue-only artifacts; commissioned with build spec in [nedschorus#13](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/13) — triggers on creating or revising a GHI, searches existing issues and pairs first, and enforces the § Project organization revision convention: edit the body, comments only for new events, never duplicate) and `md-write` (the pair), each small, embedding the zero-context-reader rule with the composed-in three-test check (subject identifiable; why stated; actionable without the conversation). The companion later gets `ghi-write`/`md-write` as Codex-side skills. Each skill build DRAINS any staged lessons that name it from the old system's memory store (skills are the trigger-bearing surface; memories only stage lessons whose home doesn't exist yet); drain is defined (package-review item 9) as: copy the lesson into the skill, verify the skill text carries it, delete the memory file AND its index line, and record the drained names in the skill-build commit — the two stores never hold the same lesson — walk-me-through builds against the accepted-behavior section of [docs/issues/9-neds-notes.md](../issues/9-neds-notes.md) — the comprehension budget, the working-review rule (classify each response accepted/rejected/revised/open; capture before advancing; revise later items when a decision changes them), and one canonical behavioral contract with thin runtime wrappers, semantic parity, shared scenario tests — and drains the three 2026-07-21 walk lessons: purpose-before-mechanism ordering for decision items; capture-the-decision-never-the-meeting; and the boss's positive length rule, in place of any not-shorter phrasing — "The target is complete and clear. Length is not the measure: never cut needed substance to be shorter, never pad to look thorough; use what completeness needs within the cap, and split when the cap is too small."

**2. Revise CLAUDE.md for them.** CLAUDE.md, per sentence: training covers it → cut; training silent → state plainly; training conflicts → NOT/DO override. No rationale, no history, present-tense truth. The seed draft is input, not the base. Line-by-line boss admission. Product: the revised CLAUDE.md.
   *processed 2026-08-06 → DONE (user-approved plan mark): the admitted five-line CLAUDE.md is live at the repo root — 21 candidate lines walked line-by-line, five admitted; grid-reviewed with every ruling recorded (admission marks: docs/drafts/claude-md-draft.md; review record: md-review-records/2026-08-06-claude-md-admitted/; inputs pair closed: nedschorus#43).*

**3. Revise the wiki for them.** The boss + new-vp walk the legacy system's pages together, eliminate roughly half; survivors cleaned for the zero-context reader, imported through the checkpoint into the Obsidian shell.

**4. Build the minimal comms bridge, tested before boot.** The two-log-file bridge between choirmaster and the old system per [comms-bridge-spec.md](comms-bridge-spec.md) (spec re-derived 2026-07-21 and package-reviewed; all rulings folded). Test: a genuinely fresh subagent, handed only the draft CLAUDE.md, uses the bridge unprompted. Unruled rider: Monitor-armed idle-wake on each side.

**5. DISSOLVED (boss-ruled 2026-08-03; number kept for reference stability) — no separate startup-instruction artifact is ever written.** The step's job is covered three ways: the WAKE is the launch prompt — step 6's launcher passes the handoff text on the command line (session start is prompt-driven; CLAUDE.md instructions do not wake a session, [nedschorus#27](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/27)); the STANDING DOCTRINE is CLAUDE.md — step 2's product, carrying the handoff pickup line; the CONTENT is the founding handoff — written last by the founding pair, read at first boot as an ordinary handoff. First boot exercises the permanent mechanism; nothing is special-cased.

**6. Set up worktree/git and populate.** The git substrate (identity, `useConfigOnly`, base config), `.claude/settings.json` (bypass permissions), the launcher scripts — contract stated here directly (package-review item 9): a fresh `claude` start AND a `claude --continue` resume (measured 2026-07-21: `--continue` keeps the session id, so the handoff read table treats a continued session as the same session), **each passing the startup prompt on the command line — instructions in CLAUDE.md do not wake a session; session start is prompt-driven (boss-tested; mechanism record on [nedschorus#27](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/27))**. The fresh-start form is the boss's pattern `claude "$(cat <handoff-path>)"` — the handoff body is the prompt; under the recycling design (2026-08-02) the supervisor's ignition prompt does the same job, naming the handoff path plus the elapsed-time line and the task count, with tasks pre-seeded before launch. With terminal focus-restore cribbed from `iterm2-open-window.sh` — the Obsidian shell with step 3's survivors, skills, CLAUDE.md — and the founding handoff written LAST by the founding pair as an ordinary committed file ([fast-handoff-design.md](fast-handoff-design.md) § The founding boot), so choirmaster's first boot is an ordinary handoff read.

**7. Pick ONE task; boot; run it; learn.** Ruled direction, CONFIRMED as the first bounded test task (walk item 15, 2026-07-25): the git foundation — the git-gatekeeper build slice (config + git-gatekeeper script with built-in checks + protection lock + workflow rules). Boot-test the delta first (find a named thing in the legacy system without writing there; use the bridge; produce a handoff — plus the founding interrogation probes: who are you; what are we building; what the legacy system is and its rules; hand off and resume; d-review a sample); every failure patches the pack. Then task 2 (standing candidate: the code-review skill), and companion admission right after the boot test passes. Candidate skills join one at a time when the running task exposes the missing decision (boot-set rule, open question 8) — the git-gatekeeper task's first expected pull is `write-test-plan` ([nedschorus#18](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/18)).

